window.docContents[130].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Session.StatementComposed/#file-Computational___Specifications___Session___StatementComposed":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Session › StatementComposed.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 567 of 690 lines trusted trust banner B3, trusted in part source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (33)def Encaps1Totalstructure RefuseStatedef onSenddef onAcceptdef onDeliverabbrev RefuseMdef refuseTransmitdef refuseChalldef refuseDeliverdef refuseInjectdef refuseCorrdef refuseCorrB0Impldef refuseCorrB0def prefixPrgAvgdef prefixPrfAvgdef prefixWireAvgdef prefixAdvAvgstructure SessionCostedReductionsdef sessionCostedReductionsBoundeddef fsAeadAuthSlotSumBounddef fsChainPrgMixtureTermdef fsSaltWireMixtureTermdef fsAeadMixtureBounddef fsAeadAuthMixtureCompBounddef refineConstdef eps0IdealUnitdef hiddenSaltMixtureBounddef fig8MixShortAuthV1def fig8MixShortPrivV1def uniformStartMixtureBoundabbrev SessionCostedReductionFamilydef SessionCostedReductionFamilyBoundeddef DhKerUniform\n\nSession-level bound terms, adversary wrapper and reduction bundles shared by the statementsTrusted in part. The theorems of Computational/Theorems/ use every definition in this file except fsAeadSlotSumBound and paramsV1, which are checked by Lean; the ones they use are part of what you must read to trust the result. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.Assembles the single-session security bound (uniformStartMixtureBound) for the Double Ratchet with SPQR V1 (paramsV1) from the bucket-partitioned ACD19 (Alwen, Coretti, Dodis, EUROCRYPT 2019) Fig. 8 authenticity and switch-back privacy bounds (fig8MixShortAuthV1, fig8MixShortPrivV1, fsAeadMixtureBound, fsAeadAuthMixtureCompBound; formally incomparable with the earlier per-cell bound, see DEV-LS31 and DEV-C14), the session-to-Fig. 8 refinement slack (refineConst, hiddenSaltMixtureBound, fsAeadAuthSlotSumBound; DEV-LS36), and the epoch-0 and uniform-start root-KDF PRG switches (eps0IdealUnit). Also defines the early-corruption refusal wrapper RefuseB0.refuseCorrB0 (DEV-LS33, DEV-LS34), ML-KEM encapsulation totality (Encaps1Total), and scalar-independent DH equality fibers (DhKerUniform).Bounds are stated over a context mixture oa : ProbComp α via prefixPrgAvg, prefixPrfAvg, prefixWireAvg, and prefixAdvAvg, and evaluated on first-order ReductionDsl.CostedReduction bundles (SessionCostedReductions, sessionCostedReductionsBounded, SessionCostedReductionFamily, SessionCostedReductionFamilyBounded; see Computational/docs/REDUCTION_DSL_TUTORIAL.md).\n\n\n\nML-KEM encapsulation totality\n\ndef Encaps1TotalL58–62 ↗#K.encaps1 succeeds on every 64-byte header (satisfied by libcrux ML-KEM-768, which checks only header length).\n\n\n\nstructure RefuseStateL68–73 ↗#Observable game-state shadow tracked by refuseCorrB0: party epochs, within-epoch indices, and in-transit (pos, ct) pairs.\n\n\n\ndef onSendL79–87 ↗#Updates RefuseState after an accepted transmit or chall returning some c.\n\ndef onAcceptL89–93 ↗#Updates RefuseState when P accepts a message at position pos.\n\ndef onDeliverL95–99 ↗#Updates RefuseState after an accepted deliver-P(c).\n\n\n\nabbrev RefuseML103 ↗#\n\ndef refuseTransmitL105–114 ↗#\n\ndef refuseChallL116–125 ↗#\n\ndef refuseDeliverL127–136 ↗#\n\ndef refuseInjectL138–147 ↗#\n\ndef refuseCorrL149–158 ↗#Locally refuses corr-B when epoch .B == 0 (DEV-LS33) or epoch .A < 10 (DEV-LS34), and forwards all other corruption queries.\n\ndef refuseCorrB0ImplL160–174 ↗#\n\ndef refuseCorrB0L176–180 ↗#Wraps A so that corr-B queries refused by noBobCorrInEpoch0 (DEV-LS33) or noBobCorrWhileAliceBelowEpoch10 (DEV-LS34) return none without querying the game.\n\n\n\nMixture averaging and SPQR V1 session bound\n\ndef prefixPrgAvgL186–188 ↗#Averages a family of PRG distinguishers D o over a prefix distribution oa.\n\ndef prefixPrfAvgL190–195 ↗#Averages a family of PRF adversaries D o over a prefix distribution oa.\n\ndef prefixWireAvgL197–202 ↗#Averages a family of wire OT-CCA adversaries A o over a prefix distribution oa.\n\ndef prefixAdvAvgL204–207 ↗#Averages a family of adversaries in an arbitrary game with coins unifSpec.\n\nstructure SessionCostedReductionsL209–317 ↗#Bundle of first-order ReductionDsl.CostedReduction programs for a single Double Ratchet + SPQR V1 session at send coins BitVec 512. Combines the SPK (spk), ACD19 Fig. 8 (fig8), and FS-AEAD (fs) reduction bundles with the session-to-Fig. 8 simulators, root-KDF PRG distinguishers, and DeliverForge authenticity reductions (challSimDF, shifted boundary cells B_cka, B_prng, B_fs, and unshifted (tL, par) buckets B_cka_u, B_prng_u, B_fs_u). ML-KEM encapsulation and decapsulation failures are excluded here and charged via MlKem.KemFailBad on the universally quantified adversary, since an existentially quantified reduction could hard-code a failing seed pair (DEV-KFF1).\n\ndef sessionCostedReductionsBoundedL319–390 ↗#Step-cost, program-size, and oracle-query bounds for all reductions in R at query budget q, epoch bound qep, FS-AEAD query bound min (2 * q) (q + 2), and cost budget ratchetCostBudget q (qep + 1). Also imposes semantic query bounds min (2 + 2 * q) (q + 3) on R.B_prng / R.B_prng_u and min (2 * q) (q + 2) on R.B_fs / R.B_fs_u.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 392–401): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.E2E.fsAeadSlotSumBound\n\ndef fsAeadAuthSlotSumBoundL403–415 ↗#Computational multi-session FS-AEAD step bound at one session: chain-PRG and salt-PRF hops on A false la, plus wire OT-CCA hops on A true la, evaluated via the two-stage direct-output reductions R.prgRedAuth and R.multiRedAuth at query fuel qR.\n\ndef fsChainPrgMixtureTermL417–425 ↗#Mixture-averaged chain-PRG advantage at hybrid hop m and query fuel qR.\n\ndef fsSaltWireMixtureTermL427–444 ↗#Mixture-averaged salt-PRF and wire OT-CCA advantage terms at hybrid hop m and query fuel qR.\n\ndef fsAeadMixtureBoundL446–456 ↗#Mixture-averaged FS-AEAD short bound across fsSlotCount q active slots plus the hoisted MAC-forgery term 4 * qd * macForgeryProb C.F.\n\ndef fsAeadAuthMixtureCompBoundL458–484 ↗#Mixture-averaged direct-output chain-PRG and salt-PRF (A false la) and wire OT-CCA (A true la) bound at one session of a multi-session authenticity telescope at query fuel qR (zero MAC term; 4 * macForgeryTerm is charged once per last-leak tL bucket outside the (t, j) sum).\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 486–489): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.E2E.paramsV1\n\ndef refineConstL491–496 ↗#Context-independent session-to-Fig. 8 refinement slack: spurious DH-step terms plus the ratchet-key collision bound (qep + 2) * (q + qep + 2) * δ.\n\ndef eps0IdealUnitL498–503 ↗#Worst-case probability that uniform PRG output passes wireMacVerifiesTest, over chain counters c < 2 ^ 32 and wire lengths ser.length < 2 ^ 32 (DEV-LS23).\n\ndef hiddenSaltMixtureBoundL505–570 ↗#Mixture upper bound on the hidden-salt refinement probe game when SPQR lacks salt binding (DEV-LS36). Integrates the DeliverForge CKA, PRF-PRNG, computational FS-AEAD (fsAeadAuthSlotSumBound at qR := min (2 * q) (q + 2)), and hoisted MAC-forgery bounds over o ← oa across shifted boundary cells (tL = some (t - 2) and tL = some (t - 3)) and unshifted (tL, par) parity buckets (B_cka_u, B_prng_u, B_fs_u), charging 4 * macForgeryTerm Z q once per boundary cell and once per (tL, par) bucket (O(qep · q · macForgeryProb) total), plus spuriousStepTerm (for forward-evicted honest wires probed after sender corruption) and (qep + 1) * (qep + 2) * δ. Excludes ML-KEM failure probabilities, which are charged at top level via the real-game bad event MlKem.KemFailBad on the universally quantified adversary (DEV-KFF1).\n\ndef fig8MixShortAuthV1L572–598 ↗#Mixture-averaged bucket-partitioned ACD19 Fig. 8 authenticity bound for (R o).simFig8 on SPQR V1, with computational FS-AEAD terms expanded via fsAeadAuthMixtureCompBound at qR := min (2 * q) (q + 2) and 8 * macForgeryTerm Z q charged once per last-leak tL bucket (4 * macForgeryTerm Z q each for honest-header and forged-header modes; DEV-LS31, DEV-C14).\n\ndef fig8MixShortPrivV1L600–627 ↗#Mixture-averaged switch-back ACD19 Fig. 8 privacy bound for (R o).simFig8 on SPQR V1, summing redCKAPriv, redCKAPrivU, and redPRNGPriv over tL and charging the tL-free fsAeadMixtureBound terms (redFSPriv and 2 * redFSPrivCoin, at qR := min (2 * q) (q + 2)) once per challenge epoch i.\n\ndef uniformStartMixtureBoundL629–653 ↗#Upper bound on the mixture-averaged sessionSchemeU game bias with SPQR V1 on RefuseB0.refuseCorrB0-wrapped adversaries: sums the ACD19 Fig. 8 authenticity and privacy bounds, refineConst, the epoch-0 and uniform-start rootKdfAsPrg advantages, and 2 * hiddenSaltMixtureBound.\n\nParameterized reduction families and DH kernel hypothesis\n\nabbrev SessionCostedReductionFamilyL657–665 ↗#Family of SessionCostedReductions bundles indexed by cryptographic primitives, identity keys, group encoding, and query budgets (qep, q).\n\ndef SessionCostedReductionFamilyBoundedL667–675 ↗#Uniform resource boundedness (sessionCostedReductionsBounded) across all parameter instantiations of D.\n\ndef DhKerUniformL677–688 ↗#Scalar-independence of DH equality fibers (Dh.dh x Q = Dh.dh x Q' ↔ Dh.dh s Q = Dh.dh s Q'), used in hop 2 to relabel the epoch-0 random function across scalars.For clamped x-only X25519 on the prime-order subgroup Pt (0 plus the (ℓ - 1) / 2 pairs {±P} of order ℓ = 2 ^ 252 + 27742317777372353535851937790883648493), every clamped scalar c = 8m (2 ^ 251 ≤ m < 2 ^ 252) satisfies gcd(c, ℓ) = 1, so Q ↦ u(c · Q) is a bijection on Pt (δ = 2 ^ (-250)). The carrier Pt must be restricted to this prime-order subgroup under clamped scalars: nonzero E[8] or twist E'[4] torsion points are annihilated by 8m (which violates dh x Q ≠ 0), mixed-order or twist cosets separate uniform Pt challenges from honest basepoint multiples in CKA.corrGame, and unclamped scalars fail at x ≡ 0 (mod ℓ).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Session/StatementComposed.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Session.StatementComposed/#file-Computational___Specifications___Session___StatementComposed"}});